{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero","id":1364178,"title":"The Psychology of a Sane Hero","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-30T09:29:09-08:00","id":1364178,"title":"The Psychology of a Sane Hero","content":"One of the things I find the most...regrettable about Beast is that the books have only noted that non-psychotic heroes exist, but not really done much to delve into their personality and how they work contra their Gaston Counterparts. Like there is one hero in Conquering Heroes who is just a mom that protects kids from the worst kind of Begotten, but I would like to see a future supplement that goes into detail about these and maybe even makes them playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T09:40:56-08:00","id":1364183,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sane&quot; and &quot;psychotic&quot; probably aren't the best words to use here.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, you might want to look at Dark Eras 2's Hunger in the Black Land when you get the chance. While brief, it discusses Oracles, ancient predecessors to Heroes. They're pretty much what you're ever going to see in terms of playable Heroes (at least until there's a Beast 1.5 or 2.0 written by people that don't agree with the design approach of keeping the antagonists more off limits).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T17:18:26-08:00","id":1364247,"title":"","content":"The impulses and archetypes that make a Hero do not make for the most socially well-adjusted of individuals. Actual monsters in the closet do not help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T18:23:19-08:00","id":1364256,"title":"","content":"There was the Silversmith in Conquering Heroes too. He functions mostly as a Hunter, mentions he used to be one, makes things for the Hunters and just deals with problems that crop up in his area. I'm pretty sure it mentions he just warns Beasts not to cause problems in his territory and if they do he kills them. Considering how many of the more sane Heroes tend to be stationary and the mention that the core had Heroes who stopped being problems just no longer seeking Beasts I feel like its a fair case to make for more sane or less antagonistic Heroes to be the ones not actually on the hunt and more just defensive.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't be too off base for a table to portray it as Heroes that give in to the Quest and start just wandering the world looking for the resonance of a Beast to slay and gain power start to lose their bloody sanity and become more psychotic and monstrous from the perspective of normal humans. So a Heroes that's anchored to a specific thing and doesn't go around questing is able to fit in more with the rest of the world. The Quest doesn't care about societal rules, moors and behaviors; so long as its destroying monsters and things causing ripples in the Primordial Dream. Much like how a Horror doesn't care about anything around the feeding so long as you're feeding it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T18:53:30-08:00","id":1364262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364247#post1364247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impulses and archetypes that make a Hero do not make for the most socially well-adjusted of individuals. Actual monsters in the closet do not help.</div> </div> </div> </div>and yet, the amount of people asking for more socially adjusted (and playable) heroes never seems to go down. and damn, it is annoying.<br /> <br /> anyway OP, the heroes that seek out beasts understandably go quite power hungry and become knight templars. having the sub conscious power to make people your unquestioning followers, combined with fighting literal nightmares come to life, simply is not good for your mental health","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T19:12:23-08:00","id":1364263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364262#post1364262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and yet, the amount of people asking for more socially adjusted (and playable) heroes never seems to go down. and damn, it is annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's the weird part where we have this game called Hunter: the Vigil for people that want to play character that struggle to fight monsters already.<br /> <br /> I get the push back in Promethean with Alchemists, because hunting Prometheans is effectively incidental for them. They're after alchemical components, one of which you need to harvest from Prometheans. <br /> <br /> High Integrity Heroes... what are you playing that isn't just playing Hunter?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T20:01:55-08:00","id":1364269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364263#post1364263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there's the weird part where we have this game called Hunter: the Vigil for people that want to play character that struggle to fight monsters already.<br /> <br /> I get the push back in Promethean with Alchemists, because hunting Prometheans is effectively incidental for them. They're after alchemical components, one of which you need to harvest from Prometheans.<br /> <br /> High Integrity Heroes... what are you playing that isn't just playing Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why* I personally don't care about playable Heroes.<br /> <br /> *realistically, one of a <i>lot</i> of reasons why","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-30-2020, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-30T21:03:20-08:00","id":1364279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364263#post1364263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there's the weird part where we have this game called Hunter: the Vigil for people that want to play character that struggle to fight monsters already.<br /> <br /> I get the push back in Promethean with Alchemists, because hunting Prometheans is effectively incidental for them. They're after alchemical components, one of which you need to harvest from Prometheans. <br /> <br /> High Integrity Heroes... what are you playing that isn't just playing Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>wish I used that lol. theres also the fact Heroes aren't the first or the last antagonists to be mostly knight templars, yet the only ones to be criticized for it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T00:04:27-08:00","id":1364291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364263#post1364263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High Integrity Heroes... what are you playing that isn't just playing Hunter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously a Hunter who's also an <b>action movie hero</b>. That's the main difference to my mind, against any of other splats or really entities in CoD a Hero is just a hunter with that action movie protagonist thing to be able to heal away anything that doesn't remove body parts or kill them.<br /> <br /> Honestly, my speculation is partially the name. Like ignore the fact that the name Hero is what the Beghotten refer to them as ironically and how the Heroes view themselves most of the time, and the word hero has a lot of baggage on it that is generally positive. So you've got a title for an entire category that defaults to a giant neon sign saying, &quot;This is the good guy, the one in the right and the one you're supposed to root for.&quot; which isn't hurt by the fact that they literally exist to fight living nightmares who feed on pain, fear, and trauma. (Beast feeding habits oversimplified, but you get the idea.)<br /> <br /> I also wonder if it isn't partially a desire to play Drizzt Do'urden's role of the lone good guy rebelling from their race of unrepentant monsters and such. Not trying to insult anyone there since I recall it being a long standing insult or something to chastise someone for playing a Drizzt clone. It just seems there was a reason the character was popular and it wouldn't surprise me if the initial presentation of Heroes as a group of unrepentatnt ego driven psychotic glory-hounds doesn't allow the Heroes that are more Hunter+ to fit that sort of niche for those looking to play in CoD.<br /> <br /> <br /> I honestly wonder, sometimes, how things would have shaken out if Heroes had been given a different name like Slayers or something.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T00:56:36-08:00","id":1364297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364291#post1364291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously a Hunter who's also an <b>action movie hero</b>. That's the main difference to my mind, against any of other splats or really entities in CoD a Hero is just a hunter with that action movie protagonist thing to be able to heal away anything that doesn't remove body parts or kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Hero's non-Beast specific powers are generally less dangerous than Endowments so... not really sure that's enough even if it might be accurate to certain motivations.<br /> <br /> Obviously Cell and Compact level play doesn't have that, but Conspiracy level Hunter play does. If I'm a vampire, I'd rather face a high Integrity Hero than TFV agent packing anti-vampire equipment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I honestly wonder, sometimes, how things would have shaken out if Heroes had been given a different name like Slayers or something. </div> </div> </div>The name part just feels so... superficial. They're called Heroes because Beast uses the monomyth as a framing device. The book isn't subtle about this. I just don't get how you get into the book far enough to know that there are the bad low Integrity Heroes, and the reasonable high Integrity Heroes, and not get that they're called Heroes because of their forced roll into an intrusive narrative, not because they're inherently good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T03:30:51-08:00","id":1364311,"title":"","content":"Also, I feel that it should be mentioned that if you feel that Hunter does not cover the themes of being an Hero which you like, there is the Dark Hero template from Mirrors which was meant for players. Sure, it would require some adjustments, as it is in 1e system, but I'm sure a number of people have made a conversion for them. So yeah, if you want to have playable Heroes you can and have some mechanical support for it, it is just that in a game focused around Beasts, it makes little sense for those who slay the protagonists of the game to be presented as playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T07:34:11-08:00","id":1364342,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth remembering that a lot of people's first impressions of Heroes are from the kickstarter draft, and because that initial impression was so poor many of them didn't bother to follow up and see how things changed in publication. Even for those that did, well, first impressions are important for a reason, they stick with you.<br /> <br /> It's unfortunate, but a lot of people were really put off by how myopic and hypocritical Beasts came across, especially given that at the time Heroes were created primarily by Beasts feeding carelessly and so many example Beasts were unrepentant monsters in the worst sense of the word. It's unsurprising to me that so many view Heroes as, if not the good guys, at least the significantly lesser of two evils.<br /> <br /> I think Beast could have benefitted greatly from more word count and editing on the topic of reduction to monomyth as a fail state. Heroes and Beasts are complex people with a wide range of values and drives, at least until the monomyth catches them up and strips them of nuance in favor of archetype.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T08:40:07-08:00","id":1364354,"title":"","content":"....like....beasts are meant to be hypocritical...they are full of shit and the world doesn't need them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T09:12:19-08:00","id":1364361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364354#post1364354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....like....beasts are meant to be hypocritical...they are full of shit and the world doesn't need them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sentiment applies to a good portion of the splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T11:29:22-08:00","id":1364377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364354#post1364354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....like....beasts are meant to be hypocritical...they are full of shit and the world doesn't need them.</div> </div> </div> </div>This does not, in exchange, mean that Heroes are morally and ethically consistent, full of roses, and needed by the world- and that's before you account that Beasts, and by comparison Heroes, are more complicated than this angle captures.<br /> <br /> Beast is a game of right bastards circling around each other in a dance of violence, but each is also a contributor to and pillar for communities, offering truths and beliefs in ways that are also uncomfortable and even compromising. The Chronicles world would probably be better on the while if both were removed, on the whole, but they are complicated enough that that's a wibbly statement.<br /> <br /> The myth of the hero is a complicated but ultimately toxic concept in the real world, but Beast has traditionally had trouble communicating that nuance in it's narrative. I have ideas on how to fix THAT problem, but for now that's one guy's fanon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-31-2020, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T11:34:56-08:00","id":1364378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364342#post1364342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's worth remembering that a lot of people's first impressions of Heroes are from the kickstarter draft, and because that initial impression was so poor many of them didn't bother to follow up and see how things changed in publication.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it?<br /> <br /> We're getting close to the 3 year mark on that (by close I mean in less than a month).<br /> <br /> I'm pretty comfortable with the response to anyone that falls back to this position being, &quot;If that turned you off the game, please move on instead of coming into a space for discussing the game and expecting your opinions to be valued when you haven't updated your knowledge of the game in this long.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this is true of the OP, because they haven't actually done this openly to my knowledge. But I'm done caring about this excuse. We have had a revised manuscript, and multiple supplements, expanding the game and improving it significantly from its flawed start. If people don't care about the game enough to know that, they don't actually care about things like what playable Heroes would actually be about either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even for those that did, well, first impressions are important for a reason, they stick with you. </div> </div> </div>But.... first impressions of Heroes don't count?<br /> <br /> The Kickstarter draft isn't exactly kind to them. It repeatedly makes it clear that they're violent hypocrites. Many Beasts might be capable of repenting but don't, while becoming a Hero means tossing the idea that you'll have to repent for anything you do out the window. The original draft makes it clear that Hunters usually think that Heroes are <b>Slashers</b> because of how far gone Heroes are to their fellow monster fighters.<br /> <br /> I'm not surprised if people consider Heroes the lesser evil, but I presume it's because they didn't read the text to have that impression. If you actually read it, even the old preview, and came off with that impression? Then yeah, I'm surprised because there's less nuance about them being anything but dangerous lunatics that gladly kill innocent humans in their quest to kill Beasts than their is in the final text. That version doesn't present Heroes as complex people once they become Heroes that all goes away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364354#post1364354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....like....beasts are meant to be hypocritical...they are full of shit and the world doesn't need them.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The world doesn't need&quot; is an empty phrase. The world doesn't need humans either. The world would continue on if we all poofed out of existence tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Beasts are actually, by default, not very hypocritical. They're presented as knowing what they are, the danger they represent, and acknowledging their desire for survival over the comfort and safety of others. They know their attempts to temper their needs via Lessons is an artificial philosophic position with no weight behind it to generate consequences for Beasts that don't serve this purpose. As the book notes in crossover with Hunter, one of the best weapons Beasts bring to conflict with hunters is their honesty about what they are, and hunters frequently not being so honest with themselves about what compromises they make.<br /> <br /> Beyond &quot;need,&quot; it seems worth expanding on an important part of the metaphysics of Beast:<br /> <br /> Humanity as a collective is what makes Beasts and Heroes.<br /> <br /> Our primordial fears create the Horrors that find dreamers to bond with to form the Begotten. Our unwillingness to confront those fears in a healthy fashion and instead seek comfort in civilization to alleviate such fears (which isn't really possible) spurned Oracles and Sages to fall from mediators between the manifestations of our fears and ourselves, into the debased glory hounds Heroes are.<br /> <br /> The world doesn't need lions, but they exist. There's lots of ways killing a lion is justifiable for humans seeking to protect themselves or other humans. But trophy hunters there to kill a lion just to kill a lion aren't doing it to make the world better.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T15:11:37-08:00","id":1364408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364378#post1364378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But.... first impressions of Heroes don't count?<br /> <br /> The Kickstarter draft isn't exactly kind to them. It repeatedly makes it clear that they're violent hypocrites. Many Beasts might be capable of repenting but don't, while becoming a Hero means tossing the idea that you'll have to repent for anything you do out the window. The original draft makes it clear that Hunters usually think that Heroes are <b>Slashers</b> because of how far gone Heroes are to their fellow monster fighters.<br /> <br /> I'm not surprised if people consider Heroes the lesser evil, but I presume it's because they didn't read the text to have that impression. If you actually read it, even the old preview, and came off with that impression? Then yeah, I'm surprised because there's less nuance about them being anything but dangerous lunatics that gladly kill innocent humans in their quest to kill Beasts than their is in the final text. That version doesn't present Heroes as complex people once they become Heroes that all goes away.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original draft (and to an extent this remains a problem in the rewrite, but at least it's acknowledged) was so obviously and heavily slanted to a Beast's POV that most of what it said could hardly be trusted to be objective. It <i>said</i> a lot of things about Heroes, but I contend that all it made clear was what Beasts <i>thought Heroes were. </i>A biased viewpoint projecting the flaws of the worst individuals onto the entire group. That's more explicitly confirmed in the final draft but it was the impression I had from first reading. <br /> <br /> Also just on a practical level Heroes didn't exist without Beasts. Their powers and obsessive drive were literally, explicitly the result of Beasts being careless. They tried to make it palatable by saying only low integrity characters could be thusly corrupted, and then bizarrely claimed it wasn't appropriate for characters who lost integrity because of supernatural trauma to become Heroes... because that's a Hunter narrative. Which it is, but that dividing line always felt like an extremely artificial distinction to avoid victim blaming, because they wanted a simple narrative that Heroes are the &quot;good guys&quot; (who are actually bad guys) rather than dealing with the more nuanced perspective that some of them might be genuinely decent people with legitimate grievances. <br /> <br /> And of course unlike Beasts they could raise their integrity and retire. Just, there are several things that make Beasts the greater threat to public safety.<br /> <br /> Anyway most of that got fixed in the published version, making my complaints irrelevant, except to my original point that there's ample basis for the impression of a text trying suspiciously hard to distinguish these guys as different -and worse than- Hunters and not making a persuasive case for why that is. It just... is. Because low integrity. That was somehow self inflicted and deserved, unlike other kinds of trauma. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T15:58:48-08:00","id":1364423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364378#post1364378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The world doesn't need&quot; is an empty phrase. The world doesn't need humans either. The world would continue on if we all poofed out of existence tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Beasts are actually, by default, not very hypocritical. They're presented as knowing what they are, the danger they represent, and acknowledging their desire for survival over the comfort and safety of others. They know their attempts to temper their needs via Lessons is an artificial philosophic position with no weight behind it to generate consequences for Beasts that don't serve this purpose. As the book notes in crossover with Hunter, one of the best weapons Beasts bring to conflict with hunters is their honesty about what they are, and hunters frequently not being so honest with themselves about what compromises they make.<br /> <br /> Beyond &quot;need,&quot; it seems worth expanding on an important part of the metaphysics of Beast:<br /> <br /> Humanity as a collective is what makes Beasts and Heroes.<br /> <br /> Our primordial fears create the Horrors that find dreamers to bond with to form the Begotten. Our unwillingness to confront those fears in a healthy fashion and instead seek comfort in civilization to alleviate such fears (which isn't really possible) spurned Oracles and Sages to fall from mediators between the manifestations of our fears and ourselves, into the debased glory hounds Heroes are.<br /> <br /> The world doesn't need lions, but they exist. There's lots of ways killing a lion is justifiable for humans seeking to protect themselves or other humans. But trophy hunters there to kill a lion just to kill a lion aren't doing it to make the world better.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/GQnsaAWZ8ty00/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T17:17:47-08:00","id":1364436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364408#post1364408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original draft (and to an extent this remains a problem in the rewrite, but at least it's acknowledged) was so obviously and heavily slanted to a Beast's POV that most of what it said could hardly be trusted to be objective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you gone back to that draft recently and really looked at that?<br /> <br /> Because the chapter specifically about running Heroes, and the chapter about running crossover with the rest of the CofD, are not burdened with a lack of clarity about what's Beast PoV, and what's authorial PoV.<br /> <br /> Or are you going to say that when the book tell us that Marian Jones will kill mundane humans that hang around supernaturals too much it's a Beast's impression of her? Are Beasts describing how hunters feel about the difficulty in knowing the difference between Heroes and Slashers? Because first impressions might stick... even if they aren't accurate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also just on a practical level Heroes didn't exist without Beasts. Their powers and obsessive drive were literally, explicitly the result of Beasts being careless. </div> </div> </div>Neither of these is accurate to the original draft either. Heroes exist without Beasts, but don't formally catalyze into one mechanically until interacting with a Beast. They can spend time knowing something is wrong, but don't know what until they witness a Beast to lay that wrongness on.<br /> <br /> The Beast doesn't have to be careless about it (that's one of those Beast PoV things). Marian Jones is a good example there. Her son turned into a Beast and did nothing careless around her besides let a [probably a vampire] sleep in his room. The sheer presence of his Horror tormented her dreams no matter how much he actually tried to distance himself from his parents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And of course unlike Beasts they could raise their integrity and retire. </div> </div> </div>Last I checked Inheritances were in the original preview too, if we want to oversimplify stuff like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just, there are several things that make Beasts the greater threat to public safety. </div> </div> </div>Who automatically draws bystanders into the fight between Beasts and Heroes?<br /> <br /> Who can, with difficulty and care, actually survive without causing lasting harm to humans if they'd just be left alone?<br /> <br /> Because... that seems like the greater danger is Heroes base on these sorts of &quot;things.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anyway most of that got fixed in the published version, making my complaints irrelevant, except to my original point that there's ample basis for the impression of a text trying suspiciously hard to distinguish these guys as different -and worse than- Hunters and not making a persuasive case for why that is. It just... is. Because low integrity. That was somehow self inflicted and deserved, unlike other kinds of trauma. </div> </div> </div>Actually the case is simple as represented by a direct mechanical difference:<br /> <br /> Heroes have Life and Legend, not Virtue and Vice.<br /> <br /> The case about them being different is that they've given into the desire to pursue their obsession with being the hero of their personal story above all else.<br /> <br /> Hunters learn the truth, and are driven to defend humanity; sometimes quite aggressively.<br /> <br /> Heroes learn the truth, and are driven to disregard nuance and kill monsters based solely on their own internal narrative; sometimes quite broadly in their definition of monster.<br /> <br /> This is in the original draft. Not enough for you or not. Not clearly enough or not. It's there if you read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T18:23:06-08:00","id":1364446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364436#post1364436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you gone back to that draft recently and really looked at that?<br /> <br /> Because the chapter specifically about running Heroes, and the chapter about running crossover with the rest of the CofD, are not burdened with a lack of clarity about what's Beast PoV, and what's authorial PoV.<br /> <br /> Or are you going to say that when the book tell us that Marian Jones will kill mundane humans that hang around supernaturals too much it's a Beast's impression of her? Are Beasts describing how hunters feel about the difficulty in knowing the difference between Heroes and Slashers? Because first impressions might stick... even if they aren't accurate.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I quite literally read it while writing the above to make sure my memory was accurate. Still open in my tabs. Marian is <i>one</i> Hero, and Thaddeus makes all of <i>two</i>. Pointing to one or two characters to make sweeping generalizations about everyone else is exactly the problem I was describing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364436#post1364436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Last I checked Inheritances were in the original preview too, if we want to oversimplify stuff like this.</span></span></span><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Inheritances aren't analogous. You end up with a Horror roaming the physical world, a Horror roaming the dreamscape, or an incredibly powerful Beast who still has to feed. Also, I can't really oversimplify heroic retirement because the entirety of the detail given is that the Hero reaches integrity five and stops doing Hero things in favor of more normal hobbies. That's it, that's all they wrote. Beasts don't ever stop needing to feed their Horrors. Inheritance doesn't change that, at least not the three we had at the start.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364436#post1364436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Who automatically draws bystanders into the fight between Beasts and Heroes?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Who can, with difficulty and care, actually survive without causing lasting harm to humans if they'd just be left alone?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Because... that seems like the greater danger is Heroes base on these sorts of &quot;things.&quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Uh, nobody to the first, and both Beasts and Heroes to the second. Heroes don't &quot;automatically&quot; recruit bystanders, it's a specific power they must first learn and then intentionally activate. A Hero who senses no Beasts in their vicinity is a Hero who has the opportunity to focus on other activities and possibly increase their integrity to the point that they can resist the call.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364436#post1364436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Hunters learn the truth, and are driven to defend humanity; sometimes quite aggressively.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Heroes learn the truth, and are driven to disregard nuance and kill monsters based solely on their own internal narrative; sometimes quite broadly in their definition of monster.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's drawing a distinction that's not at all borne out by Hunter itself. Plenty of Hunters are in it for selfish reasons, and plenty have no small trouble distinguishing monstrous appearance from monstrous behavior. Saying &quot;these guys are categorically worse than Hunters&quot; is doing a hell of a disservice to one of Hunter's main themes: the uncomfortable truth that plenty of Hunters are worse than the monsters -the people- that they hunt.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T18:30:16-08:00","id":1364447,"title":"","content":"Hunters are trauma victims with a somewhat misguided approach to recovery.<br /> <br /> Heroes are....<i>hungry</i>. Their relationship to Beasts is entirely predatorial and aggressive, often without causation.<br /> <br /> It's the role their soul called out for, resonated with, and connected to the Dreams to manifest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T19:22:01-08:00","id":1364452,"title":"","content":"slightly off topic, but in the writing in the previous drafts, is it implied or outright said like in the book we have now that nascent Heroes have an innate feeling of purposelessness before they finally come in contact with a beast?<br /> <br /> just wondering, because if it was that way in the drafts, then people cant really claim that Heroes were unfairly portrayed in the early drafts (since you know, it adds a tragic, just as much a beast, element to their existence)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T19:42:09-08:00","id":1364455,"title":"","content":"At <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> recommendation, I read the section in Dark Eras 2 about Oracles. And I can definitely see that as a decent approach to so-called \u201chigh-Integrity Heroes\u201d: that is, if you want a \u201cHero\u201d who isn't obsessed with the notion that the story revolves around <i>him</i> and that he's destined to slay a Beast, you're talking aabout something more along the lines of an Oracle, not a Hero. And <i>that</i> could potentially be something that's playable \u2014 with the very real danger that it should be all too easy to cross the line from Oracle to Hero, and difficult to go back. <br /> <br /> That said, even the Oracles have one major obstacle to being playable: everything about them is still utterly dependent on getting in the way of Beasts \u2014 most notably by applying Anathema to them. As antagonists or supporting cast in a Beast game, that's usually fine; as a playable character, it's a little too one-note.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T19:52:03-08:00","id":1364456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364455#post1364455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, even the Oracles have one major obstacle to being playable: everything about them is still utterly dependent on getting in the way of Beasts \u2014 most notably by applying Anathema to them. As antagonists or supporting cast in a Beast game, that's usually fine; as a playable character, it's a little too one-note.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey look, another reason I'm not personally interested in making playable Heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T20:09:34-08:00","id":1364458,"title":"","content":"And a reason to point people towards Hunter... because Heroes are about getting in the way of Beasts mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T22:35:28-08:00","id":1364471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364452#post1364452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">slightly off topic, but in the writing in the previous drafts, is it implied or outright said like in the book we have now that nascent Heroes have an innate feeling of purposelessness before they finally come in contact with a beast?<br /> <br /> just wondering, because if it was that way in the drafts, then people cant really claim that Heroes were unfairly portrayed in the early drafts (since you know, it adds a tragic, just as much a beast, element to their existence)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd have to check the old draft to be sure, but I don't think so. It feels more true to me (that such was not the case) because I recall part of the problem was that there was a table in the draft that had a dramatic failure option ,which was used for an example, of causing whoever the Beast was feeding on at the time to become a Hero.* Now I will grant its possible its in there and I'm forgetting it. The dramatic failure can just as easily be interpreted as &quot;Okay the complication for this is your attack ends up being that part in the character's backstory that follows the sentence 'I was a normal person until one day...' so good luck when the dude comes after you later.&quot; As easily as it could be that being bitten by a werewolf or zombie in movies turns you into one, but being devoured by one does not, consequently you bite this person and they became a Hero.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Presumably this only applies if your feeding method didn't involve killing the person, though I admit I am all over pissed off undead hunting the players because they screwed up feeding that badly despite disemboweling their victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":".  terminology mix up 02-01-2020, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T23:25:44-08:00","id":1364481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364456#post1364456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey look, another reason I'm not personally interested in making playable Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough \u2014 though it does get rather grating to constantly be hearing variations on the same theme (\u201cplayable Heroes bad\u201d) over and over. (Note: this was my first post to the Beast forum in what has probably been years; and the first response I got was an utterly dismissive one. It doesn't feel good.)<br /> <br /> I do get it, though: to you, any thread that seeks to subvert the subversion of the Hero (or seems to) is probably just as grating. Personally, I'm not trying to do that \u2014 but I <i>would</i> like to see how far from the \u201cmurder-hobo\u201d the Hero (or Oracle) can get and still be thematically consistent with Beast. <br /> <br /> As I see it right now, Beast operates on the notion that the Hero/Beast dynamic is dysfunctional. Got it. But what would it look like if it <i>wasn't</i> dysfunctional? I think that's what the Oracle stuff in DE2 was trying to address: the <i>proper</i> role of a \u201cHero\u201d isn't to wantonly slaughter Beasts; but what <i>is</i> he supposed to be doing? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364458#post1364458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And a reason to point people towards Hunter... because Heroes are about getting in the way of Beasts mechanically.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll know more once Hunter 2e is in my hot little hands; but I'm thinking that a sort-of \u201ccrossover splat\u201d could be devised by way of an Oracle-like Hunter Conspiracy, with an Endowment inspired by what Oracles can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-31T23:51:31-08:00","id":1364484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364481#post1364481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough \u2014 though it does get rather grating to constantly be hearing variations on the same theme (\u201cplayable Heroes bad\u201d) over and over.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, it isn't &quot;playable heroes bad,&quot; but rather, &quot;playable Heroes aren't Heroes.&quot;<br /> <br /> If this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what would it look like if it <i>wasn't</i> dysfunctional? I think that's what the Oracle stuff in DE2 was trying to address: the <i>proper</i> role of a \u201cHero\u201d isn't to wantonly slaughter Beasts; but what <i>is</i> he supposed to be doing? </div> </div> </div>Was actually the thrust of these threads, it would be less grating on both sides. The problem is that the game already has a fairly strong answer to this (that Oracles expand on rather than add to the game). The Sages/Oracles/whatever avoided the intrusion of the monomyth so they could craft stories that would contain Beasts. Effectively, they're the source of Lessons in Beast culture, because that's how Beasts were kept in balance with humanity by Oracles/etc. back in the day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll know more once Hunter 2e is in my hot little hands; but I'm thinking that a sort-of \u201ccrossover splat\u201d could be devised by way of an Oracle-like Hunter Conspiracy, with an Endowment inspired by what Oracles can do. </div> </div> </div>I don't think you'd need to wait for HtV 2e to try this, even though it's next week and all.<br /> <br /> Giving Hunters the power to inflict Anathema on Beasts might be a bit much in keeping the line between Hunters and Heroes (or pre-Heroes) as a thing, and perhaps cut out some good drama.<br /> <br /> An Endowment that allows a Hunter group to detect and exploit existing Anathema but not place them might be more interesting because it puts them at the whims of Heroes to maximize their effectiveness against Beasts that need to get put down.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T00:06:05-08:00","id":1364486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364481#post1364481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it right now, Beast operates on the notion that the Hero/Beast dynamic is dysfunctional. Got it. But what would it look like if it <i>wasn't</i> dysfunctional? I think that's what the Oracle stuff in DE2 was trying to address: the <i>proper</i> role of a \u201cHero\u201d isn't to wantonly slaughter Beasts; but what <i>is</i> he supposed to be doing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Interpreting omens, counseling mortals, and otherwise managing the task of keeping up the passive separation between the human herd its supernaturally-empowered fears made flesh, which unfortunately does not make for great radio without breaking at least part of Beast's thesis re: &quot;Heroes are not metaphysically important to Beasts themselves except by imposition.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a game to be played where the modern dynamic between Beasts and Heroes involves a lot of battling for control of the narrative through managing relationships and manipulating social geography, but mechanically, that game is not the one we currently have the tools for; presumably in an edition of Chronicles where resonance and the various societal game-structures are more closely integrated into the core this would be easier to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T12:05:02-08:00","id":1364577,"title":"","content":"Here's two other possibilities I can see for sane hero.<br /> <br /> First, moderation and principal. Much like a Hunter, a Hero could cleave to an idea. Their Hero senses tell them when someone has suffered by a beast's hand. They try to cause more good than harm. They don't unduly risk others. They're not glory hounds by nature. And perhaps, even, they allow a Beast who is trying to minimize the harm they inflict to live, perhaps even seeing them as a person. The one that just ripped an arm off that high school student? Yeah, he's ending up six feet under.<br /> <br /> Second, the Hero as a judge. A Hero possibly who tries to convince Beasts to moderate their actions. To be as human. And they strike if they refuse their advances. A Hero could even be an ally to a Beast who's been trying to moderate their actions. Perhaps a Hero even visits the Beast's own depredations upon them if they insist, but the Hero isn't quite ready to swing a sword... unless, of course, the Anakim needs to pushed ahead of them. Perhaps even a system for asserting their authority over a beast to get gifts. Or at least, perhaps, the Hero can recover Integrity for free that way, as the idea they can peacefully get that.<br /> <br /> Or, as one more idea for a system change? A Hero who works peacefully can recover Integrity over 10, and perhaps gain powers the higher it goes. Heroes that slay Beasts are like Heracles or Odysseus, strong but fatally flawed. Heroes of Integrity are different. They may be a little more than human - they might have had to slay an unredeemable Beast. But they more than make up for it with their Wisdom. They're more than able to see past fear. Nightmares have no purchase on them. A Hero of Integrity is David facing Goliath - throwing warning shots before their faith or wisdom delivers a killing blow. They tame dragons, rather than slay them.<br /> <br /> In short, you have Beasts that cling to their Life and Beasts that revel in their Legend. Why not have Heroes who act the same way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T12:19:30-08:00","id":1364580,"title":"","content":"It would be nice if Beast had more Antagonists and Allies that fit into the game's framework.<br /> <br /> The only reason, it seems to me, to change Heroes away from what they are to is to make use of the word &quot;Hero&quot;. I just don't see the value in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T14:01:03-08:00","id":1364602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzauri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364577#post1364577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one that just ripped an arm off that high school student? Yeah, he's ending up six feet under.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of thinking, while hard to get past, would be something such a character would need to fight against.<br /> <br /> Absolutism is the enemy of the nuance needed to moderate between Beasts and humanity. What if the kid they hurt was a bully and the Beast was trying to make them feel the pain they inflicted on others? Ripping an arm off is an excessive response, yes, but it's a Beast that's still trying to moderate their actions. The willingness to engage with that sort of nuance and avoid the simple cultural norms/stories/taboos that prejudice thinking would be essential as at least an ideal to strive for. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364580#post1364580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be nice if Beast had more Antagonists and Allies that fit into the game's framework.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we've got a good deal at this point, esp. if you're playing Beast and other supernaturals are NPCs brought in under the game's framework instead of mixed games.<br /> <br /> What I'd like to see most in this regard is a book focused on the Primordial Dream and playing in human dreams, as actual locations. This opens up more space for dealing with entities residing in them for Beasts to interact with, as well as something that could be used to adjust the stakes of existing character types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T14:31:28-08:00","id":1364609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364602#post1364602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we've got a good deal at this point, esp. if you're playing Beast and other supernaturals are NPCs brought in under the game's framework instead of mixed games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know there's the whole crossover thing... But just speaking of Beast, there's....<br /> <br /> Heroes... Insatiable... as Antagonists. There's Primordial Cultists, potentially being Allies or Antagonists... Other Beasts of course, as other Allies or Antagonists... <br /> <br /> Excluding other gamelines and just focusing on Beast: The Primordial, am I missing what else there is?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364602#post1364602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'd like to see most in this regard is a book focused on the Primordial Dream and playing in human dreams, as actual locations. This opens up more space for dealing with entities residing in them for Beasts to interact with, as well as something that could be used to adjust the stakes of existing character types.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would dearly love a Beast: The Primordial book focused on exploring human dreams, the Primordial Dream and the Astral Realm overall as a Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T15:06:17-08:00","id":1364614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tzauri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364577#post1364577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's two other possibilities I can see for sane hero.<br /> <br /> First, moderation and principal. Much like a Hunter, a Hero could cleave to an idea. Their Hero senses tell them when someone has suffered by a beast's hand. They try to cause more good than harm. They don't unduly risk others. They're not glory hounds by nature. And perhaps, even, they allow a Beast who is trying to minimize the harm they inflict to live, perhaps even seeing them as a person. The one that just ripped an arm off that high school student? Yeah, he's ending up six feet under.<br /> <br /> Second, the Hero as a judge. A Hero possibly who tries to convince Beasts to moderate their actions. To be as human. And they strike if they refuse their advances. A Hero could even be an ally to a Beast who's been trying to moderate their actions. Perhaps a Hero even visits the Beast's own depredations upon them if they insist, but the Hero isn't quite ready to swing a sword... unless, of course, the Anakim needs to pushed ahead of them. Perhaps even a system for asserting their authority over a beast to get gifts. Or at least, perhaps, the Hero can recover Integrity for free that way, as the idea they can peacefully get that.<br /> <br /> Or, as one more idea for a system change? A Hero who works peacefully can recover Integrity over 10, and perhaps gain powers the higher it goes. Heroes that slay Beasts are like Heracles or Odysseus, strong but fatally flawed. Heroes of Integrity are different. They may be a little more than human - they might have had to slay an unredeemable Beast. But they more than make up for it with their Wisdom. They're more than able to see past fear. Nightmares have no purchase on them. A Hero of Integrity is David facing Goliath - throwing warning shots before their faith or wisdom delivers a killing blow. They tame dragons, rather than slay them.<br /> <br /> In short, you have Beasts that cling to their Life and Beasts that revel in their Legend. Why not have Heroes who act the same way?</div> </div> </div> </div>This post has me thinking along a different line: namely, Heroes and their like as the ChroD counterpart to Hunter: the Reckoning. The point of similarity is that both are people who have become supernaturally aware of monsters, and have to decide how they'll respond to that. <br /> <br /> Heroes are like the Zealous: they fight the monsters: avengers, defenders, and judges. Oracles are like the Visionary, seeking to understand the monsters. Carrying the parallel further, maybe there's another type, akin to HtR's Merciful (innocents, martyrs, and redeemers) who see their role as minimizing the damage that Beasts do. <br /> <br /> Hmm\u2026<br /> <br /> Or perhaps a more correct analogy is that Heroes are Waywards, Oracles are Visionaries, and the third time would be Hermits. Those three Creeds were defined as the ones who were most directly influenced by Vision, a supernatural awareness of the monsters. If Heroes are Waywards (relatively speaking), then some of the more sane mindsets for, well, not exactly Heroes but others of their kind might be analogous to Avengers, Defenders, and Judges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-01-2020, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T15:39:23-08:00","id":1364623,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a>, beasts have all the Incarnates as possible enemies and allies too. I could say vampire only has Strix, revenants, cults. but that's ignoring Drauger and belials brood (which are both vampires in essence)<br /> <br /> also <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, I too would like more on exploring the dream realms (and would really help how the Horror ties into the actions of a beast. like the corporate ravager. how does his Horror tie into the Myth he has made)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T16:04:18-08:00","id":1364629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364623#post1364623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar851_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"851\" data-vbnamecard=\"851\">Paradim</a>, beasts have all the Incarnates as possible enemies and allies too. I could say vampire only has Strix, revenants, cults. but that's ignoring Drauger and belials brood (which are both vampires in essence)</div> </div> </div> </div>Those're still Beasts, tho! ^.^<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how well Changeling or Promethean fare either... Kinda seems like Werewolf is the one most spoiled for options... Maybe I'm wrong, though...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T16:11:55-08:00","id":1364631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364629#post1364629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those're still Beasts, tho! ^.^<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how well Changeling or Promethean fare either... Kinda seems like Werewolf is the one most spoiled for options... Maybe I'm wrong, though...</div> </div> </div> </div>oh I know they are still beasts, that's why I mentioned the other vampire antagonists. for promethean, we have pandorans (by proxy what that combined pandoran thing is called), sublimati, centimani, alchemists, and quashmallin. changelings have true fae, Huntsman, Hobgoblins, the factions of antagonist changelings, and hedge queens<br /> <br /> and I would say Hunters are tied with werewolves for the most spoiled in enemies lol<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh crap, and while I would like more on it, promethean has The Jovian","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-01-2020, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T16:15:48-08:00","id":1364632,"title":"","content":"Changeling has Gentry, Huntsmen, Fetches, Hobgoblins, and Hedge Ghosts. <br /> <br /> Promethean has Alchemists, <i>qashmallim</i>, Pandorans, Sublimati, Centimani, Praecipatus, clones, and the Jovian.<br /> <br /> Beasts do seem to be a little starved for diversity in its antagonists in comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-01-2020, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T17:55:11-08:00","id":1364650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364632#post1364632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling has Gentry, Huntsmen, Fetches, Hobgoblins, and Hedge Ghosts.<br /> <br /> Promethean has Alchemists, <i>qashmallim</i>, Pandorans, Sublimati, Centimani, Praecipatus, clones, and the Jovian.<br /> <br /> Beasts do seem to bad a little starved for diversity in its antagonists in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>The general lack of attention to the Dreamborn and the things that can happen when they and the Astral bubble up into reality is one big problem, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T18:26:16-08:00","id":1364660,"title":"","content":"Right. As things stand right now, the only place you'll find the Dreamborn is in the Player's Guide \u2014 and in the Mage 1e supplement Astral Realms. I'd definitely be up for a Beast supplement (or a Beast/Changeling supplement?) addressing the Dream, both Bright and Primordial.<br /> <br /> In terms of the notion of playable Heroes (or whatever), something like this would help mitigate the issue I mentioned earlier about Heroes being excessively one-note: it would be possible, in theory, to run a story featuring a Hero/Oracle/whatever who never once encounters a Beast, and instead deals exclusively with Dreamborn: you'd just need to expand his abilities to apply to Dreamborn as well as Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-01-2020, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T20:27:35-08:00","id":1364679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364660#post1364660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. As things stand right now, the only place you'll find the Dreamborn is in the Player's Guide \u2014 and in the Mage 1e supplement Astral Realms. I'd definitely be up for a Beast supplement (or a Beast/Changeling supplement?) addressing the Dream, both Bright and Primordial.<br /> <br /> In terms of the notion of playable Heroes (or whatever), something like this would help mitigate the issue I mentioned earlier about Heroes being excessively one-note: it would be possible, in theory, to run a story featuring a Hero/Oracle/whatever who never once encounters a Beast, and instead deals exclusively with Dreamborn: you'd just need to expand his abilities to apply to Dreamborn as well as Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>But heroes ARENT one note, and they come into being when a beast causes a ruckus. and a Hero would be having an extremely hard time just getting to a dream born, let alone being aware of it.<br /> <br /> it just seems like willing ignorance to say heroes are one note. they have a much better write-up in the corebook, INCLUDING one sample Hero trapped in a coma, and we have the examples in Night Horrors Conquering Heroes. at this point, it's like saying Predator Kings are one note since I just read the corebook saying &quot;they hate human civilization&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T20:43:56-08:00","id":1364681,"title":"","content":"They're \u201cone-note\u201d in the sense that all of their specials are explicitly geared toward Beasts. Well, other than being Hard to Kill. Heroic Tracking and Heroic Stalking? Only work vs. Beasts. Anathema? Can only be placed Beasts. Gifts? Nearly all of them only trigger when dealing with a Beast; the biggest exception (if you want to call that) is Kinslayer, which only works on non-Beasts who have (wait for it\u2026) Family Ties to a Beast. Advancement? The only way to acquire more Gifts is\u2026 to kill a Beast. Sensing a theme here? If you want to use a Hero for anything other than messing with Beasts, you have a guy who is Hard to Kill and who probably has Followers. <i>Within the context of being a pain in the rear for Beasts,</i> Heroes can be quite diverse. Outside of that role? There's almost nothing to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T21:11:07-08:00","id":1364685,"title":"","content":"This doesn't surprise me at all. Heroes are specifically designed to be antagonists for Beasts...<br /> <br /> The name of the game is Beast: The Primordial. Everything about that game, should be focused around Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T21:35:01-08:00","id":1364687,"title":"","content":"Yep. But it <i>does</i> make it hard to use Heroes in any other way. That's not a situation you have in any other game, for the most part: if you want to throw goblins up against your vampire protagonists, there are no particular difficulties in doing so. Have a storyline in mind featuring an alchemist against changelings? No problem. Want a ghost to haunt your mummy? Easy. In contrast, the only thing a Hero has any edge against is a Beast. Which, if that's how you like it, is fine. But it <i>is</i>, comparatively, one-note. And if I happen <i>not</i> to like it, I can:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Avoid Beast<br /> \u2022 Put up with it<br /> \u2022 Change it<br /> <br /> I'm exploring the third option right now. But I'm trying to do so in a way that remains as consistent as possible with Beast. <br /> <br /> So can we please not have these \u201cHeroes should only be good for one thing\u201d potshots? As I said in my first post here, it's grating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T21:43:44-08:00","id":1364689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364681#post1364681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're \u201cone-note\u201d in the sense that all of their specials are explicitly geared toward Beasts. Well, other than being Hard to Kill. Heroic Tracking and Heroic Stalking? Only work vs. Beasts. Anathema? Can only be placed Beasts. Gifts? Nearly all of them only trigger when dealing with a Beast; the biggest exception (if you want to call that) is Kinslayer, which only works on non-Beasts who have (wait for it\u2026) Family Ties to a Beast. Advancement? The only way to acquire more Gifts is\u2026 to kill a Beast. Sensing a theme here? If you want to use a Hero for anything other than messing with Beasts, you have a guy who is Hard to Kill and who probably has Followers. <i>Within the context of being a pain in the rear for Beasts,</i> Heroes can be quite diverse. Outside of that role? There's almost nothing to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will say I have myself complained that while Beasts work well in crossovers, Heroes themselves have a limited crossover capacity with other games, and a lot of this ties into that.<br /> <br /> The center of their conflict should always be with Beasts, but Some Diversification is not a bad thing. A Hero should be a decently viable sideways antagonist to throw in most games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T21:59:17-08:00","id":1364692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364689#post1364689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say I have myself complained that while Beasts work well in crossovers, Heroes themselves have a limited crossover capacity with other games, and a lot of this ties into that.<br /> <br /> The center of their conflict should always be with Beasts, but Some Diversification is not a bad thing. A Hero should be a decently viable sideways antagonist to throw in most games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well... Hrm. That is definitely valid... I mean, if a Hero is fighting a Beast that has Kin involved, the Hero should be a viable threat against the Kin as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T22:44:09-08:00","id":1364696,"title":"","content":"A simple (and possibly overpowered?) fix would be to let Gifts work against all sorts of monsters, not just Beasts; and then retool Kinslayer to be less about making Gifts useful at all against non-Beasts and more about giving some special edge when Family Ties are involved. <br /> <br /> Kinslayer might still be the only way to use Heroic Tracking and Heroic Stalking against someone who isn't innately tied to the Primordial Dream (e.g., Beasts and Dreamborn). Also, maybe Kinslayer <i>could</i> allow the Hero to place an Anathema on those with Family Ties; but for them, the Anathema always manifests as its Low-Satiety effect (so they're generally not as effective), and the Anathema is temporary, going away at the end of the scene (or maybe chapter? I'm spitballing here). <br /> <br /> That would maintain the desired feel that becoming Kin to a Beast makes you especially vulnerable to a Kinslayer Hero, while greatly opening up the possibilities available to all Heroes. That said, I <i>wouldn't</i> let a Kinslayer gain new Gifts by killing Kin. <i>That</i> would remain a Beast-only thing; not even most Dreamborn would count, although larval Horrors might \u2014 they are, after all, nascent Beasts. <br /> <br /> And making \u201ckill a Beast\u201d the <i>only</i> way to gain Gifts makes things needlessly difficult for the likes of Sleeping Beauty; there should be other ways to gain them. I'm not sure what those other ways might be; only that they ought to be harder to accomplish than killing a Beast is, and/or not the sort of thing that the usual Hero would think of. I'm perfectly fine with the Hero-as-foil <i>thinking</i> that the only way to grow more powerful is to kill Beasts. But Sleeping Beauty ought to be able to grow without having to slaughter Beasts in order to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T23:09:55-08:00","id":1364699,"title":"","content":"I thought Sleeping Beauty <i>was </i>killing Beasts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T23:13:00-08:00","id":1364700,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm misremembering. I was thinking that she has mainly been serving as a guide to others in the Primordial Dream, and not actively seeking out and destroying Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 02-02-2020, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T23:23:31-08:00","id":1364702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364700#post1364700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm misremembering. I was thinking that she has mainly been serving as a guide to others in the Primordial Dream, and not actively seeking it and destroying Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I picked it back up to double check... And... her entry is kind of confusing to me. She somehow chased a Horror in her dreams into it's Lair and killed the Horror there, which is how she got stuck in a coma. But then says she can't follow Horrors back to their Lairs, and has to just point other Heroes in the right direction.... somehow...<br /> <br /> Then says &quot;with each victory, Melanie grows stronger.&quot; But she's not getting victories? I mean, the rules are explicit that only the Hero who strikes the killing blow will earn a new Gift.<br /> <br /> So, over all, this is weird to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-01T23:26:16-08:00","id":1364703,"title":"","content":"Anyways, Sane Heroes.<br /> <br /> Assuming a Hero doesn't transcend their condition somehow, the most sane Hero I can think of is one who steps up primarily to a Beast who's being right jackass and tries to get them back onto the program-and making that clear, that means acknowledging that both are icons that guide the masses in terms of aspiration and rejection, and therefore <i>not</i> killing all but the most egrigious of Beasts and otherwise smacking them around a bit to soften the ego, and then working to impart some wisdom to Beasts so that they may be better wisdom dispensers themselves. Violence may be a part of their lives, but like the better Beasts in their community, good Heroes understand that they have the power to impart strong values to others through their actions, and iron can sharpen iron without breaking the other. THe pagentry of the conflict between Beasts and Heroes can be very powerful and beneficial stuff, but it works best when it's not done to fill a hole in their lives and under assumption of the worst of their opponents. Heroes build both regular humanity and Beasts (and maybe even other monsters) in the same way a truly transcendent Beast will do for all of the above.<br /> <br /> Both Beasts and Heroes are, ultimately, meant to be metaphorical guides for the masses, and they are at their best when they strip the ego, work to really understand everyone, and are willing to make themselves object lessons without murdering each other for it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364699#post1364699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Sleeping Beauty <i>was </i>killing Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>She <i>does</i>, but the entire thing is a lot more tangled.<br /> <br /> But in regards to her becoming more powerful, well-she may not be getting Gifts, but she's def getting EXP and broad knowledge, and that still helps with the work of Waking The Fuck Up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 02-02-2020, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T05:17:42-08:00","id":1364737,"title":"","content":"One thing I've looked at for making Heroes more varied and crossover friendly is minor templates. It's not too hard to imagine a Hero desperate for more power opting to get Lost Boy augments, and Conquering Heroes had a Proximi and a Hunter.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, it would be pretty cool to have a Hero end up as a Deviant in pursuit of more power. They'd stop being a Hero mechanically but if their conviction touchstones are Beasts and allies of Beasts it makes for a pretty smooth transition and opens up their options a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T05:56:32-08:00","id":1364741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364681#post1364681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're \u201cone-note\u201d in the sense that all of their specials are explicitly geared toward Beasts. Well, other than being Hard to Kill. Heroic Tracking and Heroic Stalking? Only work vs. Beasts. Anathema? Can only be placed Beasts. Gifts? Nearly all of them only trigger when dealing with a Beast; the biggest exception (if you want to call that) is Kinslayer, which only works on non-Beasts who have (wait for it\u2026) Family Ties to a Beast. Advancement? The only way to acquire more Gifts is\u2026 to kill a Beast. Sensing a theme here? If you want to use a Hero for anything other than messing with Beasts, you have a guy who is Hard to Kill and who probably has Followers. <i>Within the context of being a pain in the rear for Beasts,</i> Heroes can be quite diverse. Outside of that role? There's almost nothing to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>ahh ok, my bad. yeah I can agree. Heroes should have some abilities to challenge other templates","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 02-02-2020, 09:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T23:00:57-08:00","id":1364951,"title":"","content":"I suppose my question is, what's the gameplay goal from playable Heroes? What do you want a session of &quot;<i>Beast: The Primordial</i>, but y'all can be Heroes if you want&quot; to look like?<br /> <br /> Do you want a group of all Heroes? Do you want a mixed group of Heroes and Beasts? Other splats? Do you just want the players to kill Beasts?<br /> <br /> This is a game that's designed from the ground up to be about Beast player characters, and Heroes are designed from the ground up as antagonists to <i>Beast player characters</i>. It's in the mechanics, the story and the base assumptions about the game.<br /> <br /> You can argue about viewpoints and semantics and writing and subjective morality all that stuff, but, ultimately, games are meant to be played. So, why should someone <i>play </i>a Hero?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-02T23:42:47-08:00","id":1364953,"title":"","content":"Why you have rules to play Seers in Mage corebook? Why you have those for Hosts, Pure or spirits? Cause full dementional antagonists need proper mechanics and broader view point. Like classic say - <i>'good antagonist is just hero of story you do not understand, yet'.</i><br /> <br /> Heroes should not be defined only by their obsession with Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 02-03-2020, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T00:29:37-08:00","id":1364956,"title":"","content":"Also, fetches. <br /> <br /> And even if you <i>don't</i> allow anyone to play a Hero, wyrdhamster's point holds. Frankly, it's not really about \u201cplayable Heroes\u201d so much as it's about \u201ccomplex and interesting Heroes\u201d \u2014 which has the <i>side effect</i> of making them playable. Personally, I entered this thread not to discuss making Heroes more palatable, but to consider <i>variations on Heroes</i> such as the Oracles from Dark Eras 2. Heck, the core rulebook says that <i>they exist</i>; it's just that they tend not to cross paths with Beasts. That further implies that it's possible to be a (variant of a) Hero without everything you say or do being focused on Beasts. <br /> <br /> And frankly, Beasts aren't immune to becoming self-centered egotists, either: every so often, they too need to be reminded that it's not all about them. And arguments to the effect of \u201cthis game is called \u2018Beast\u2019\u201d tend to miss that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T00:36:30-08:00","id":1364958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364689#post1364689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will say I have myself complained that while Beasts work well in crossovers, Heroes themselves have a limited crossover capacity with other games, and a lot of this ties into that.<br /> <br /> The center of their conflict should always be with Beasts, but Some Diversification is not a bad thing. A Hero should be a decently viable sideways antagonist to throw in most games.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a random thought, I feel that to a Hero, all supernatural beings that step up to him are Beasts, and he engages them as such, as hero of his tale. He can\u2019t be the aggressor in this story, as that wouldn\u2019t make him the hero, but if he\u2019s in a vampire\u2019s territory and it decides to stalk him, it\u2019s a beast. If he\u2019s with his family and werewolves begin hassling them, they\u2019re beasts and suffer the weight of the anathema he brings to bear. <br /> <br /> But these are only lesser minions sent to trouble the Hero while he hunts his true foe, the Beast itself. The Hero can hunt the Beast as that\u2019s the story. But these lesser creatures only make themselves his enemies when they stand in his way. Of course, smart Heroes figure this out and can twist the narrative to be deliberately provocative, essentially forcing other creatures to notice him, and he feels the invigoration of anathema power as those beings decide to hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T02:08:21-08:00","id":1364971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364953#post1364953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why you have rulrs to play Seers in Mage corebook?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different developers have different approaches is a main reason.<br /> <br /> That said, there are 12 pages of just mechanics on running Heroes in Beast core. It's not like there aren't rules for them.<br /> <br /> Could you remind me where there are rules for Seers of the Throne that abandon the Exarches but maintain all of the perks of being a Seer? Or the rules for the Pure regaining their Auspices? Or the XP charts for playable spirits?<br /> <br /> The existence of rules for things doesn't inherently change their role in their games. That the Seers (who are just mages with a different default philosophy and some friends in high places for it) could be played with the rules provided doesn't mean how they act given they're servants to the Exarchs goes poof.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cause full dementional antagonists need proper mechanics and broader view point. </div> </div> </div>Besides seeing themselves as the enemies of Beasts, the extant mechanics allow for an extremely wide variety of view points from Heroes as it is. Saying they can't be full dimensional antagonists because of their obsessions with Beasts is like saying vampires can't be full dimensional characters because of their obsession with drinking blood. Having a defining concept doesn't mean they're flat and uniform.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like classic say - 'good antagonist is just hero of stpry you do not understand, yet'. </div> </div> </div>Which is, quite literally, the core of Heroes as it is. It's actually not a good piece of writing advice, because plenty of antagonists are not deluded about what they are (Freddy Krueger is not the hero of a story you do not understand, and he'd probably be offended if you suggested he was). The horror genre esp. is full of compelling antagonists that might be sympathetic in someway, but never fit into this mold of &quot;hero of their own/another story.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Heroes should not be defined only by their obsession with Beasts. </div> </div> </div>They're not?<br /> <br /> For example, Heroes have a Life and Legend, which helps define what of their life before remains a core part of them, and how they connect to the Primordial Dream; not Beasts directly.<br /> <br /> Even their abilities aren't all Beast focused. Their power to gather followers around them just gathers followers. If we're going to talk about Heroes and non-Beast supernaturals, the Followers section points out that the call a Hero puts out for Followers can flip some of them into Hunters. That's actually an incredibly potent ability that doesn't directly relate to Beasts at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364956#post1364956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even if you <i>don't</i> allow anyone to play a Hero, wyrdhamster's point holds. Frankly, it's not really about \u201cplayable Heroes\u201d so much as it's about \u201ccomplex and interesting Heroes\u201d \u2014 which has the <i>side effect</i> of making them playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are the current rules for them unable to generate complex and interesting antagonists? The idea that &quot;complex and interesting&quot; inherently makes them playable doesn't hold up at all to the large number of interesting and complex unplayable antagonists in the CofD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That further implies that it's possible to be a (variant of a) Hero without everything you say or do being focused on Beasts. </div> </div> </div>It's possible to be a normal Hero that's already like this. There's a sample Hero that targets all supernaturals rather than just Beasts.<br /> <br /> What any variant on Heroes can't do, is break their connection to the Primordial Dream, which means they can never fully escape the presence of Beasts as the other main critter around with that same bond.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And frankly, Beasts aren't immune to becoming self-centered egotists, either: every so often, they too need to be reminded that it's not all about them. And arguments to the effect of \u201cthis game is called \u2018Beast\u2019\u201d tend to miss that point. </div> </div> </div>That's a serious non-sequitur.<br /> <br /> The books are abundantly clear that plenty of Beasts deserve getting smacked down (or harsher) for what they do, and that their need to control their own story leads them towards being self-centered.<br /> <br /> The &quot;this game is called Beast&quot; has nothing to do with that point, and everything to do with the number of people that seem obsessed with tossing the core of the game out for whatever they want to shove into its place.<br /> <br /> You're missing the context vastly worse than anyone saying it is missing any point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T02:19:08-08:00","id":1364972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What any variant on Heroes can't do, is break their connection to the Primordial Dream, which means they can never fully escape the presence of Beasts as the other main critter around with that same bond. </div> </div> </div> First off, nobody's suggesting that Heroes should break their connection to the Primordial Dream. But also, Beast itself already states that there are Heroes who Beasts rarely if ever encounter; and they're generally the \u201csane\u201d ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T02:43:36-08:00","id":1364973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364953#post1364953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why you have rulrs to play Seers in Mage corebook? Why you have those for Hosts, Pure or spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Heroes, Seers, Hosts, Pure and spirits all have rules. Only Seers and Pure have rules meant to be <i>playable</i>, and they're both just the antagonist version of the splat you're supposed to be playing anyway. (And Pure had to wait for a supplement in second edition.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T03:33:32-08:00","id":1364980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364972#post1364972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But also, Beast itself already states that there are Heroes who Beasts rarely if ever encounter; and they're generally the \u201csane\u201d ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're also the narratively boring ones; outside of (oh look at this...) using them to subvert the expectations of Beasts that expect their enemies to be the normal type of Heroes in the game.<br /> <br /> The Heroes the book says exist it also says it doesn't bother putting on screen for a reason. The Good Hero that uses their connection to the Primordial Dream to find people that really need help and get them to come to support group meetings isn't really the jumping off point for a good story if they don't want to go out and do more with that connection because they know it risks losing themselves towards less altruistic and productive efforts (and that self awareness, not sanity, is actually the key difference). Their stagnation in this regard is what keeps them good, but also keeps them from being fun to play.<br /> <br /> Changing that requires either changing their connection to the Primordial Dream, or changing how they can interact with Beasts.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> For a more pop culture reference point here.<br /> <br /> A Good Hero is like playing Bruce Wayne who never puts on the cowl and becomes Batman, and instead figures out after a bit of vigilante crime fighting, that he's punching crooks because of his personal issues, and he can actually make the world better by being a wealthy philanthropist instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 02-03-2020, 06:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T06:37:00-08:00","id":1364998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364958#post1364958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a random thought, I feel that to a Hero, all supernatural beings that step up to him are Beasts, and he engages them as such, as hero of his tale. He can\u2019t be the aggressor in this story, as that wouldn\u2019t make him the hero, but if he\u2019s in a vampire\u2019s territory and it decides to stalk him, it\u2019s a beast. If he\u2019s with his family and werewolves begin hassling them, they\u2019re beasts and suffer the weight of the anathema he brings to bear.<br /> <br /> But these are only lesser minions sent to trouble the Hero while he hunts his true foe, the Beast itself. The Hero can hunt the Beast as that\u2019s the story. But these lesser creatures only make themselves his enemies when they stand in his way. Of course, smart Heroes figure this out and can twist the narrative to be deliberately provocative, essentially forcing other creatures to notice him, and he feels the invigoration of anathema power as those beings decide to hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This is similar to how I've hacked my Heroes to work as.<br /> <br /> At my table, Heroes can apply Anathema to all supernaturals who share a Kinship with the Beast they're hunting, but also get to do so to those who attack them regardless of a Begotten's role in the events.<br /> <br /> By going after a Hero, supernaturals become part of The Narrative<span style=\"color:#3C4043\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2122 and the confrontation between them and the Hero becomes part of his saga (at least for what concerns the forces that empower the Hero and probably the Hero himself, depending on his attitude &amp; morals). Not the central one, not the most glorious one, not the <i>primordial </i>one, perhaps, but the practical result is there. And yes, smart ones can provoke that. After all, if monsters decide to attack you because they want to take you out, from a symbolic point of view they're creatures coming after you because your heroic nature is a menace to them and their schemes<br /> <br /> It also helps to tighten the threat they pose to Beasts and their allies both in crossover games or not.<br /> <br /> &quot;Don't worry about this Hero, my dear dragon friend. Stay here and we'll kill him for you. That wooden bat he wields is no threat to us&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Yes, it is</i>&quot;</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T07:46:26-08:00","id":1365008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1364998#post1364998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">This is similar to how I've hacked my Heroes to work as.<br /> <br /> At my table, Heroes can apply Anathema to all supernaturals who share a Kinship with the Beast they're hunting, but also get to do so to those who attack them regardless of a Begotten's role in the events.<br /> <br /> By going after a Hero, supernaturals become part of The Narrative<span style=\"color:#3C4043\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u2122 and the confrontation between them and the Hero becomes part of his saga (at least for what concerns the forces that empower the Hero and probably the Hero himself, depending on his attitude &amp; morals). Not the central one, not the most glorious one, not the <i>primordial </i>one, perhaps, but the practical result is there. And yes, smart ones can provoke that. After all, if monsters decide to attack you because they want to take you out, from a symbolic point of view they're creatures coming after you because your heroic nature is a menace to them and their schemes<br /> <br /> It also helps to tighten the threat they pose to Beasts and their allies both in crossover games or not.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Don't worry about this Hero, my dear dragon friend. Stay here and we'll kill him for you. That wooden bat he wields is no threat to us&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;<i>Yes, it is</i>&amp;quot;</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>my only issue with that is, to me, it takes away from the unique conflict beasts have within themselves. if Heroes can apply Anathema to just anything that attacks them, then just about all supernaturals understand the suffering of the monomyth. in my opinion, that really takes away from Beast and makes all supernaturals closely related to the primordial dream (since that's how beasts get anathema in the first place)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T08:40:03-08:00","id":1365017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1365008#post1365008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">my only issue with that is, to me, it takes away from the unique conflict beasts have within themselves. if Heroes can apply Anathema to just anything that attacks them, then just about all supernaturals understand the suffering of the monomyth. in my opinion, that really takes away from Beast and makes all supernaturals closely related to the primordial dream (since that's how beasts get anathema in the first place)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that the Anathema are very much a Beast thing, as they're directly tied to the Horror itself. Beasts are also only susceptible when Sated. How does that translate to other supers?<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of other supers being able to stumble into The Narrative*. Instead of placing Anathema, you could extend Gifts that normally only applies to Beasts to the new target (perhaps with reduced efficiency, if possible), as well as use the Wits+Empathy roll (with appropriate penalty) for finding preexisting Anathema to find out one of the target's Banes or Bans, if they have any. As an ST I'd go for the ones that are easiest to weaponise or otherwise use to your advantage.<br /> <br /> *Personally I'd frame it so it's less that the non-Beast supernatural creature gets pulled in into some metaphysical narrative, and more that it's the Hero that extends their nature when finding an appropriate opponent. As such it would only happen during significant circumstances. Perhaps it could be determined by a roll, modified by circumstances and whether it resonates with their Legend or Life.<br /> Or perhaps it's something that only happens to a small subset of Heroes that are subject to some quirk in their nature as a Hero. Maybe some Heroes resonate closely with vampires and can spend a WP to &quot;pull in&quot; any vampire they find. Maybe the most &quot;successful&quot; Heroes build up a Legend that has started to hunger for the blood of monsters, any monsters, allowing the Hero to go after <i>anyone</i> they deem monstrous enough (nudge-nudge, wink-wink).<br /> Either way, my idea is for Gifts to work on the target not because the target is weak to them, but because Gifts are part of the Hero and it's the Hero that is modified to be able to use them against a non-Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T09:19:33-08:00","id":1365022,"title":"","content":"I rather like the thought of a Hero being able to quickly identify pre-existing weaknesses or qualities that affect a supernatural creatures behavior. Like being able to tell what sets a werewolf off to go into death rate really fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T09:22:51-08:00","id":1365024,"title":"","content":"There's the Kinslayer Gift to consider, too. <br /> <br /> I like the idea that monsters who aggress against a Hero become vulnerable to his Gifts; but I'd reserve Anathema for Beasts, with Kinslayer being retooled to extend them to monsters with Family Ties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T09:32:59-08:00","id":1365027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1365017#post1365017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree that the Anathema are very much a Beast thing, as they're directly tied to the Horror itself. Beasts are also only susceptible when Sated. How does that translate to other supers?</div> </div> </div> </div>To get more into details, my personal solution is for some Gifts to apply (those easier to weaponise you mention, like Vanquisher's Strength and Champion's Endurance, as they are more on the &quot;Hero's own strength&quot; side of thing) and for Atavisms to consider monsters with Kinship to a Beast as if they're Middle Satiety and those who came looking for trouble as Low Satiety. No High Satiety except against Beasts, as usual, and no Anathema whatsoever if the Hero is fighting monsters by his initiative without a Begotten being part of the picture.<br /> <br /> The whole thing is basically a counterpart to Kinship, which works only for those monsters who enter the Narrative either as obstacles to the monster slayer or &quot;minions and allies&quot; of the big final monster at the end of the hunt.<br /> <br /> But that power does not come from the supernaturals themselves: it comes from the Hero. Beasts are related to monsters through the Primordial Dream &amp; the Dark Mother. Heroes are the nemesis of the Begotten and. as such, they have a degree of influence over other monsters, though much more limited by the Monomyth and the structures of the Astral.<br /> <br /> If it sounds <i>wrong</i>, that's because it's intentional. Inside a game where Beast are involved, either crossover or not, it shows Family what the deal with Heroes is, gives them a bitter taste of the monomyth, and tests the bonds of Kinship they have.<br /> <br /> There's<i> lots </i>more I have to say on the matter, if anyone's interested. Though I probably should make another thread for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":"02-03-2020, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-03T09:39:00-08:00","id":1365031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1364178-the-psychology-of-a-sane-hero?p=1365027#post1365027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To get more into details, my personal solution is for some Gifts to apply (those easier to weaponise you mention, like Vanquisher's Strength and Champion's Endurance, as they are more on the &amp;quot;Hero's own strength&amp;quot; side of thing) and for Atavisms to consider monsters with Kinship to a Beast as if they're Middle Satiety and those who came looking for trouble as Low Satiety. No High Satiety except against Beasts, as usual, and no Anathema whatsoever if the Hero is fighting monsters by his initiative without a Begotten being part of the picture.<br /> <br /> The whole thing is basically a counterpart to Kinship, which works only for those monsters who enter the Narrative either as obstacles to the monster slayer or &amp;quot;minions and allies&amp;quot; of the big final monster at the end of the hunt.<br /> <br /> But that power does not come from the supernaturals themselves: it comes from the Hero. Beasts are related to monsters through the Primordial Dream &amp; the Dark Mother. Heroes are the nemesis of the Begotten and. as such, they have a degree of influence over other monsters, though much more limited by the Monomyth and the structures of the Astral.<br /> <br /> If it sounds <i>wrong</i>, that's because it's intentional. Inside a game where Beast are involved, either crossover or not, it shows Family what the deal with Heroes is, gives them a bitter taste of the monomyth, and tests the bonds of Kinship they have.<br /> <br /> There's<i> lots </i>more I have to say on the matter, if anyone's interested. Though I probably should make another thread for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>well I'm interested, and initially, I thought you just meant anathema could be applied, no strings attached (also, how was writing Mummy)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member